{% comment %}
  Four facts a stranger needs before mailing us irreplaceable film.

  Everything here is already true and already stated somewhere on the site —
  the problem is that a first-time visitor has to go looking. Turnaround lives
  in the announcement bar, delivery and storage are buried in FAQ rows on the
  service pages, and the drop box is only mentioned on the mail-in page.

  Turnaround is deliberately NOT restated with a number. The announcement bar
  is the single place the lab keeps that current, and a second copy on the home
  page would be the one nobody remembers to update.

  Usage:
    {% render 'cfl-trust-band' %}
{% endcomment %}

<ul class="cfl-trust" role="list">
  <li class="cfl-trust__item">
    <span class="cfl-trust__label">Developed daily</span>
    <span class="cfl-trust__body">
      C-41 and black &amp; white run every day. Current turnaround is posted at the top of
      this page.
    </span>
  </li>
  <li class="cfl-trust__item">
    <span class="cfl-trust__label">Drop off or mail in</span>
    <span class="cfl-trust__body">
      Tampa drop box out back, or send film from anywhere in the country.
    </span>
  </li>
  <li class="cfl-trust__item">
    <span class="cfl-trust__label">Scans over Google Drive</span>
    <span class="cfl-trust__body">
      A private link by email, kept live for a year so you can download on your own time.
    </span>
  </li>
  <li class="cfl-trust__item">
    <span class="cfl-trust__label">Free shipping over $100</span>
    <span class="cfl-trust__body">
      On anything we send you: film, cameras, gear and your negatives coming home.
    </span>
  </li>
</ul>
